{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q25080072","formula":"C₁₁H₁₆BrNO₃","hill":"C11H16BrNO3","elements":["H","C","N","O","Br"],"composition":{"C":11.0,"H":16.0,"N":1.0,"O":3.0,"Br":1.0},"names":{"en":"2-bromomescaline"},"descriptions":{"en":"2-Bromomescaline (2-BM or 2-Br-M), also known as 2-bromo-3,4,5-trimethoxyphenethylamine, is a putative psychedelic drug of the scaline family and derivative of the phenethylamine hallucinogen mescaline which has an unusual 2-bromo substitution. It is an agonist for serotonin receptors, with a binding affinity of 215 nM at 5-HT1A, 513 nM at 5-HT2A and 379 nM at 5-HT2C, so while it is around 10 times more tightly binding than mescaline at 5-HT1A and 5-HT2A receptors, it is over 20 times more potent at 5-HT2C. The drug was 5-fold more potent in substituting for LSD than mescaline in rats. It is not known to have been tested in humans."},"fame":2,"pubchemCid":16637783,"mass":290.15,"charge":0,"smiles":"COC1=C(C(=C(C(=C1)CCN)Br)OC)OC","inchikey":"UXQBKANLBLUVMK-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-(2-bromo-3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)ethanamine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"16637783","atoms":32,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.729,"y":2.626,"z":-0.57,"el":"Br"},{"x":1.334,"y":2.401,"z":-0.332,"el":"O"},{"x":1.686,"y":-2.353,"z":-0.099,"el":"O"},{"x":2.876,"y":0.146,"z":-0.118,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.846,"y":-0.593,"z":0.758,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.252,"y":-0.202,"z":-0.411,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.733,"y":-0.382,"z":-0.514,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.657,"y":1.06,"z":-0.422,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.461,"y":-1.345,"z":-0.303,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.405,"y":-0.39,"z":0.866,"el":"C"},{"x":0.729,"y":1.178,"z":-0.324,"el":"C"},{"x":0.925,"y":-1.228,"z":-0.204,"el":"C"},{"x":1.52,"y":0.034,"z":-0.215,"el":"C"},{"x":1.526,"y":3.035,"z":0.93,"el":"C"},{"x":0.999,"y":-3.602,"z":-0.096,"